\title{lagpower: genetic lag time and power to detect population differentiation}
\description{
When a genetic study finds no population structure, three explanations
compete:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{lag time}: the populations split too recently for drift to have
changed allele frequencies detectably (the "grey zone");
\item \strong{low power}: the markers or sample sizes are too limited;
\item \strong{genuine connectivity}: gene flow keeps the populations homogeneous.
}
}
